He wasn't talking about lawfulness---if you're neutral, many gnomes
and elementals are peaceful to me.  And you still can't kill them
without decreasing your alignment.  (Chaotic is sort of different,
since you *can* kill peaceful creatures without getting your god
upset.)

The point is that you can't really help it.  Your pet decides what it
likes to kill.  It's not like you can give command to your pet to kill
that dwarf that just picked up $10000 you dropped.

If you can order your pet to kill someone in particular, then I agree
it shouldn't attack peaceful creatures.  The way it is now, it should
attack peaceful creatures (note "peaceful" is only against you, and it
means nothing to your pet) if it feels like to be consistent.

